# Azure Multi-Region Resilient Infrastructure

## 🚀 Project Overview
I designed and deployed a globally redundant cloud infrastructure in Microsoft Azure to ensure 99.99% availability. This project simulates a production environment for a high-traffic application where downtime is not an option.

## 🏗️ Architecture Components
- **Global Load Balancing:** Azure Front Door (Standard)
- **Compute:** 2x Azure Static Web Apps (East US 2 & West US 2)
- **Networking:** Virtual Network (VNet) Peering for cross-region communication
- **Governance:** Resource Locks and regional Resource Group isolation (https://github.com/egaines1/azure-multi-region-resilient-infrastructure/blob/main/1%20Creation%20of%20Resource%20Groups%20and%20Resource%20Locks.PNG?raw=true)

## 🛠️ Challenges & Solutions
- **Quota Limitations:** Encountered a 0-vCPU limit for standard App Services. **Solution:** Pivoted to a serverless architecture using Static Web Apps to bypass hardware constraints while reducing cost.
- **Provider Registration:** Fixed `MissingSubscriptionRegistration` for `Microsoft.Cdn` by manually registering the resource provider in the subscription settings.
- **Propagation Delay:** Managed global DNS sync times (~20 mins) for Front Door endpoints, verifying backend health via direct endpoint testing.

